SUMMARY:(FULL) Everything Book Club\, "The Sum of Us" by Heather McGhee
DESCRIPTION:Join this session as part of our community read and receive a 
 free copy of "The Sum of Us: What Racism Costs All of Us and How We Can 
 Prosper Together" while supplies last\, thanks to Partners for Health 
 Foundation! For more details and related events\, go to Montclair Reads 
 "The Sum of Us." The community read will culminate with a live Open Book / 
 Open Mind author conversation with Heather McGhee on Tuesday\, October 13 
 at 7 p.m. \n\nIf you’re sick of the antagonism and zero-sum-game thinking 
 so prevalent in American public life today\, you’ll find a refreshing 
 antidote in this still timely landmark bestseller from 2021. What if we've 
 been thinking about opportunity in America all wrong? What if instead of 
 groups trying to get a larger slice of the pie\, we all worked together to 
 create a bigger\, better pie? Economist Heather McGhee goes on a road trip 
 across the country asking "why can't we have nice things?" and is surprised 
 to encounter in a variety of towns\, workplaces and houses of worship what 
 she calls "the Solidarity Dividend"—what we gain when people come 
 together across race and other differences to accomplish what we simply 
 can’t do on our own. Could we find it in our own hometown? \n\n“Every 
 so often a book comes along that seems perfectly timed to the moment and 
 has the potential to radically shift our cultural conversation. [The Sum of 
 Us] is one of those books.—Chicago Tribune \n\nHeather McGhee is an 
 expert in economic and social policy. The former president of the 
 inequality-focused think tank Demos\, McGhee now chairs the board of Color 
 of Change\, the nation’s largest online racial justice organization. \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-16782098
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16782098
END:VEVENT
