SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] Google Maps (Senior Planet AARP lecture)
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nVisit sites around the world from 
 the comfort of your home\, get a bird’s-eye-view of your childhood 
 neighborhood\, or simply get directions to your friend’s house! Google 
 Maps is a mapping application that offers satellite imagery\, street maps\, 
 and street-view perspectives. It also has a route planner for your 
 preferred transportation method\, be it foot\, car\, bicycle or public 
 transportation. During this lecture\, you’ll get an introduction to the 
 platform and a demonstration of how to use it.\n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis 
 class is run by the MILL. Please register for classes directly through 
 their website here.\n\nFor questions about MILL classes please call 
 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL @ MPL is made possible through a partnership between 
 the MILL\, Montclair Public Library and Partners for Health.
