DTEND:20260826T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260826T000000Z
SUMMARY:Unearthing Stories of Female Artists in Exile and Resistance
DESCRIPTION:Session 2 of a two-part series on Billie Holiday. Join us for a 
 discussion of her landmark 1956 autobiography\, marking its 70th 
 anniversary. Written with journalist William Dufty\, Lady Sings the Blues 
 is a raw and unflinching account of Holiday's life — her rise as one of 
 jazz's greatest voices\, her struggles with racism\, addiction\, and 
 exploitation\, and her refusal to be silenced. Participants receive a copy 
 of the book\, available for pickup at the Main Branch. Light refreshments 
 provided. Part of Adult Summer Reading 2026: Unearth a Story.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10306-17066105
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17066105
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260826T210000Z
DTEND:20260826T221500Z
DTSTAMP:20260826T000000Z
SUMMARY:Silent Book Club Montclair
DESCRIPTION:At Silent Book Club® there's no assigned reading. SBC members 
 gather in bars\, cafés\, bookstores\, libraries\, and online to read 
 together in quiet camaraderie. All readers are welcome—ebooks or 
 audiobooks\, poetry or prose\, fiction or non-fiction... it's 
 BYOBook.\n\n\nDid you love silent reading time in school? Are you more of 
 an introvert that loves books\, but doesn't want to jump into a discussion 
 group? Are you looking to read more\, but struggle to sit down and just DO 
 IT? If you answered 'yes' to any of these\, you might like Silent Book 
 Club! Each month\, we meet around Montclair and enjoy each other's company 
 with a book of our own choosing.\n\nRegistration is required. We will be 
 meeting at Porter Park in Montclair for all summer meetings! In the event 
 of rain\, an alternate location will be chosen.\n\nPlease be advised this 
 book club will be meeting at a public location and therefore cannot 
 guarantee a quiet reading environment. This book club is best for readers 
 who enjoy a coffeeshop ambiance (low chatter\, music\, outside noise\, 
 etc.) or those who prefer to read with headphones.
LOCATION:Montclair - Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Club
UID:LibCal-10306-15514069
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15514069
END:VEVENT
