 Times Book Review Book Club. \n\nGoes with the Open Book / Open Mind 
 program with Tayari Jones about "Kin" the following week on Tuesday\, 
 September 15! Tickets cost $35 and include a signed copy of the book. (If 
 for any reason you can't afford a ticket\, come talk to me.)\n\nWe'll talk 
 about Jones's conversation as well as "Kin\," a poignant historical novel 
 set in the civil rights era about two motherless childhood friends who take 
 very different journeys: one to the storied HBCU Spellman College\, the 
 other to make her way in the world. \n\nTAYARI JONES is the author of four 
 others novels\, most recently the New York Times bestseller "An American 
 Marriage\," which was an Oprah’s Book Club selection and also appeared on 
 Barack Obama’s summer reading list and his year-end roundup. It won the 
 Women’s Prize for Fiction\, the Aspen Words Literary Prize\, and an NAACP 
 Image Award and has been published in two dozen countries. Jones is the 
 C.H. Candler Professor of English and Creative Writing at Emory University 
 and lives in Atlanta.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-17281137
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17281137
END:VEVENT
