SUMMARY:60th Anniversary of MLK in Montclair - Film Screening and Discussion
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School event. .\n\nThe Rev. Dr. Martin 
 Luther King Jr\, visited Montclair High School on Sept. 11\, 1966 to speak 
 at the retirement of Rev. D.C. Rice\, pastor of Union Baptist Church and an 
 early mentor. A planned ceremony at Montclair High school was met with 
 community uproar\, leading to two separate King speeches on school 
 grounds.\n\nWe will recognize the 60th anniversary of this event with a 
 film screening of about Dr. King followed by a discussion and Q&A moderated 
 by Dr. Leslie Wilson of Montclair State University.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-16803076
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16803076
