BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260915T223000Z
DTEND:20260916T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260915T000000Z
SUMMARY:Open Book / Open Mind\, Tayari Jones\; "Kin"
DESCRIPTION:NEW VENUE! If you're going to buy the book anyway\, why not see 
 the author in conversation at the Library this fall? You can pick up your 
 copy of the book at Watchung Booksellers the first week in March. Tickets 
 cost $35 and include a signed copy of the book. The event will take place 
 at the Unitarian Universalist Congregation at Montclair. Register now at 
 tinyurl.com/OBOMTJones\n\nCo-presented by the Montclair Alumnae Chapter of 
 the Delta Sigma Theta Sorority. \n\nAn instant New York Times bestseller 
 and a selection for both Oprah's Book Club and The New York Times Book 
 Review Book Club.\n\nNew York Times bestselling author Tayari Jones ("An 
 American Marriage") will be talking about her Oprah's Book Club pick "Kin" 
 with her fellow novelist and former student Cleyvis Natera ("The Grand 
 Paloma Resort"). In the heyday of the civil rights era\, two motherless 
 childhood friends from Honeysuckle\, Louisiana\, find themselves taking 
 very different paths. \n\n“'Kin' is the kind of all-encompassing reading 
 experience I’m always hoping to find: smart and funny and deftly 
 profound. This is Tayari Jones’s very best work.” —Ann 
 Patchett\n\n\n\nDoors open at 6 p.m. The discussion will be followed by an 
 audience Q&A and book sales and signing with Watchung Booksellers. \n\nOpen 
 Book / Open Mind is sponsored by Montclair Public Library Foundation\, 
 Watchung Booksellers\, Anonymous\, David and Mary Lee Jones\, and our 
 individual Underwriters. We are also grateful for the generous support of 
 our in-kind sponsors\, First Congregational Church of Montclair\, The 
 George\, and Amanti Vino. To support Open Book / Open Mind and other 
 library programs\, click here to donate.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Open Book / Open Mind
UID:LibCal-10306-16256515
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16256515
END:VEVENT
