SUMMARY:Make Something Book Club
DESCRIPTION:Love books and making things? Join the Make Something Book 
 Club\, a relaxed gathering where participants can chat about the books 
 they're currently reading while working on a creative project. Bring your 
 knitting\, crocheting\, needlepoint\, embroidery\, cross-stitch\, 
 quilting\, or other portable craft and enjoy conversation with fellow 
 readers and makers.\n\nThere is no assigned book—everyone is welcome to 
 share what they're reading\, discover new titles\, and connect with others 
 in the community while creating something by hand.\n\nBring a project 
 you're working on\, or start something new! Thanks to generous donations 
 from our community\, we'll often have a small selection of craft supplies 
 available to share\, though materials will vary from meeting to meeting. If 
 you have a specific project in mind\, we encourage you to bring your own 
 supplies.\n\nFeel free to drop in! Registration isn't required\, but 
 signing up is the best way to stay informed about any schedule changes\, 
 cancellations\, or other program updates.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Arts & Crafts, Book Discussion, Book Club
