BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261007T220000Z
DTEND:20261007T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20261007T000000Z
SUMMARY:Breaking the Silence: Understanding Depression\, Suicide\, and the Power of Connection
DESCRIPTION:Presentation by Dr. Jason Dean and Dr. Rae Dumont\n\nDepression 
 is often misunderstood\, accompanied with shame\, secrecy or blame. So is 
 suicide. The impact a loss by suicide has on friends and family is 
 enormous. Without open conversations\, people often feel alone as they 
 carry the memory and question themselves about what they might have done to 
 help. \n\nThis presentation\, in the context of a rising incidence of 
 depression\, anxiety and suicide\, aims to offer understanding and 
 compassion for people who struggle with mental illness. It  offers insights 
 and comfort to those who have loved a person with depression\, and tried to 
 help. \n\n \n\nThere will be ample time for discussion and for 
 questions.\n\n \n\nRae Dumont\, MD\, LMFT\, is both a pediatrician and a 
 family therapist. While she practiced and taught at Harvard Medical 
 School\, she focused on the impact of one person's illness through the 
 entire family\, and on the interconnection between mental and physical 
 health. \n\nIn her family therapy practice\, she helped people navigate 
 difficulties by collaborating\, rather than becoming divided. \n\nShe is 
 also a mother\, a widow\, and a friend to many. She now turns her 
 experiences into words that speak of resilience\, and the flawed road 
 toward becoming good enough. In her fiction\, she finds a personal\, 
 intimate voice\, which connects emotionally with her readers’ 
 humanity.\n\nIn the Shadow of Silence\, (2-17-2026) is a novel about love\, 
 family life\, and depression. She hopes for it to bring insight and comfort 
 to her readers. \n\n \n\nJason Dean\, MD is a child and adult psychiatrist 
 and founder of The Center for Developmental Psychiatry\, a group practice 
 in Teaneck\, NJ. He is also a Clinical Instructor at Yale School of 
 Medicine.\n\nIn his clinical work\, he has worked to integrate a 
 biological\, medical view of psychiatry with a psychological perspective. 
 Dr. Dean hopes to augment the discussion with insight gained from his 
 clinical experience and training\, as well as his work with families of 
 individuals struggling with depression.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Health & Wellness, Personal Growth
